A vintage 1970s spy-thriller movie poster aesthetic depicting a brass skeleton key transforming mid-air into streams of glowing encrypted data ribbons, set against a deep navy background with aged paper texture and film grain. The key floats above an antique wooden desk scattered with manila folders and a rotary telephone. Warm amber lighting casts dramatic shadows while teal digital particles spiral around the key like protective magic. The composition uses a Dutch angle for tension, with vignette darkening at the edges typical of period photography.
